<title>UK: Bass rebounds as OFT rumours lift shares.</title>
<headline>Bass rebounds as OFT rumours lift shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK brewer Bass rebounded amid rumours that the UK competition watchdog, the Office of Fair Trading (OFT) would soon make a favourable recommendation on Bass' proposed takeover of Carlsberg-Tetley, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1042 GMT, the shares were up 15-1/2p to 783p.</p>
<p>Concerns the OFT would refer the takeover to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission have pressured the shares in recent week.</p>
<p>Shares also got a boost from talk Kleinwort Benson told clients to buy the stock, they said.</p>
<p>The brokerage couldn't be reached for comment.</p>
</text>
